# NOTICE — vendor/tecno/TECNO-KI5m

The binaries under `proprietary/` are copied byte-for-byte from the stock
TECNO KI5m (UMS9230) firmware, build GL-20240612V218. No patching, repacking
or re-signing was applied.

Per-file provenance: `blobs.sha256` (sha256 + path), `inventory/stock.tsv`
(type, mode, uid, gid, size, sha256, link target), `provenance.json`.

## What is known

- Source: vendor partition of the V218 `super.img`; the extracted `vendor_a`
  is byte-identical to the stock `vendor.img` (841748480 B, sha256
  `fed3cf42…7207`).
- Owners of the vendor payload are TECNO / Transsion, Spreadtrum/Unisoc, and
  the respective silicon and component vendors (ARM, Imagination, NXP,
  Silead, Goodix, DTS, Dolby and others present in the tree).
- The tree also contains AOSP/Lineage-derived runtime artifacts as shipped by
  the OEM. Those are not relicensed here.

## What is not claimed

- No license text is shipped per blob; the exact license of each OEM binary is
  not published in the firmware and is therefore unknown here.
- `prebuilt/inspection/` is metadata extracted from the same image for audit
  (VINTF/SELinux), not a build input.

## Exclusions

22 paths that the build regenerates are listed in `inventory/exclusions.tsv`
with the file that generates each. The raw `vendor.img` is not committed.
